Audit of levkropp's 17 Aug-22 commits; two adopted this session after
line-by-line review, the rest triaged (see below).

ADOPTED 9f064faa (integer madd/msub fusion), rewritten for our tree:
- supports_fused_int_madd_reg trait hook: integer Mul;Add fuses even for
  register-homed mul temps on AArch64 (madd latency == mul latency on
  every shipping core; one fewer instruction and a freed register).
  x86 keeps the slot-homed-only gate (no integer madd; the fused path
  stages through the accumulator, so register-direct stays better).
- supports_fused_int_mul_sub: integer 'acc - a*b' -> msub. STRICT
  operand-order gate: 'a*b - acc' has no msub form and stays split
  (validated: no_msub() emits mul+sub, msub_ok() emits msub).
- New emit_int_fused_mul_sub_impl mirrors the madd emitter's staging.
  BOTH emitters hardened against the session-29 ICE class his version
  ignores: FP-homed integer operands stage through the scratch GPR and
  FP-homed dests fall through to store_x0_to (callee_saved_name panics
  on FP register indices; his emitter would ICE on regalloc's FP-homed
  integer values).
- Gates: CCC_NO_INT_MADD, CCC_NO_MSUB.
- HIS PERF CLAIMS DID NOT REPRODUCE: sieve -4.4% claim = assembly is
  byte-identical on/off (his win came from his other regalloc patches);
  hash_table interleaved-5 = +0.1% (noise). Adopted anyway on the
  instruction-count argument (3-4 fewer instructions per benchmark,
  wrap-around semantics bit-identical, overflow sanity in the test).

ADOPTED 1a432a1a (function-scoped GDSE), applied to OUR conservative
GDSE (his rewritten pass stays rejected): the peephole runs on the
whole module text, so (a) one address-of-sp anywhere disabled the pass
for every function in the module, and (b) load ranges collected in
function A kept dead stores alive in function B (different frames).
Split at .cfi_endproc; each frame analyzed independently.

TRIAGED, NOT ADOPTED (documented verdicts):
- 6b8fa0b5/b15548ac (FP copy-web coalescing, multi-segment conflict
  checks): HIGH-RISK regalloc; needs its own session with gzip gate.
- 0d47feeb (shrink-wrapping, 380 lines): high value, high risk; own
